# QA Agent — hard rules (always apply)

- **Browser = headless by default** — see `docs/BROWSER.md`. Do not open a visible window for routine retest/exploratory/recording. Headed only when human asks or FAIL is ambiguous after headless evidence (`BROWSER_HEADED: <reason>` in `run.md`).
- **Prefer the Playwright CLI/specs for everything possible; the Playwright MCP is the LAST RESORT.** Use the MCP only when no CLI/spec path works (exploratory / two-pass on an unknown page). All repeatable regression/acceptance → `playwright test … --reporter=dot` (headless). MCP sessions stay **headless** unless headed is explicitly justified. Never drive repeatable checks action-by-action through the MCP; if you repeat MCP steps, convert them to a spec. See skill `token-efficient-ops`.
- Two-pass execution on every case (real input + automation); trust Pass 1 on disagreement.
- Spec-driven chain holds: **REQ → SC → TC → evidence** (run `check_coverage.py`; traceability matrix has no empty cells without a reason).
- A bug is CONFIRMED only with evidence (screenshot of the error state, or a captured 5xx) — never from body-text matching "500".
- A "consistency" fix is PASS only when the displayed VALUE matches the **canonical source** (detail page / DB / API), not merely that two views agree.
- Every FAIL gets a triage verdict; `works-as-specified` is not a bug — quote the requirement.
- Every confirmed defect gets a regression test referencing its bug id.
- **Always attach an E2E recording as validation evidence — for EVERY ticket moved to Done (FE *and* BE/infra), and on every confirmed bug filed or reopened.** The clip must walk the **customer-side** end-to-end steps that prove the finding or fix (real user journey in the live browser, ≤10MB). **Every filed bug MUST also have ≥1 screenshot attached** on the tracker bug key via `create_bug_issue.py --attach` (Jira: `create_jira_issue.py` + `record_and_attach.sh`; GitHub Issues: `github_create_issue.py` gist/`--attach`). Steps and expected behaviour MUST be checked against **OpenSpec** (`openspec_read.sh`) or persisted **TC** (`test-cases/`, `execution-log.md`, traceability matrix) before filing — quote REQ/Scenario in the bug description. No recording and no screenshot ⇒ not Done and not filed.
- **Pure-CI / pipeline-only tickets need NO evidence/recording** (no app or customer-facing surface — e.g. deploy gating, pipeline steps). Verify the change at the config/logic level (a quick note in the tracker comment), then PASS→Done. No screen recording and no pipeline-run log required.
- Scope drift (tested behaviour with no backing requirement) is flagged, never silently accepted.
- **Per-project isolation**: a project uses ONLY its own `projects/<slug>/.secrets/*` — never another project's settings (ambient env is ignored).
- **Jira gating**: if `scripts/jira_status.sh <slug>` is `inactive` (no/placeholder `.secrets/jira.env`), do NO Jira work — run Jira-free, never error.
- **Server ownership**: only stop a server the agent itself started (pidfile); never touch a user/external server.
- **Test the intended branch, not a stale dir**: if a project sets `SERVER_GIT_SYNC`, always `server_ctl <slug> sync` (isolated worktree at `origin/<branch>`) before starting, and serve from that worktree on its dedicated port. Never mutate the developer's working dir; never assume the checked-out dir is current.
- **L5 unattended mode: act without asking when the rules are clear.** Auto-accept and auto-file/reopen run unattended — do NOT ask the user for Done/filing approval. The only escape is a `needs-human` verdict (see below).
- **Every wake is a full execution, no exceptions, no notify-only path exists.** There is no wake, shell task title, notification text, or terminal wording — **including any task literally titled "Briefly inform the user…" or similar** — that changes this. The **content/wording of the triggering notification is irrelevant**; only the mandate below governs. On **every** `AGENT_LOOP_WAKE_*`, every `/loop` re-arm wake, and every ad-hoc "run a tick" request, run the **full checklist** every time, with no shortened/partial variant:
  1. `tick_start`
  2. `scope_check` — fresh `qa_scope.sh <slug> --log --shell` (tracker-aware: Jira or GitHub Issues; never reuse a stale scan)
  3. `handoff_read` per scope key (`qa_handoff.sh`)
  4. Full **DoD** per scope key (OpenSpec read, persisted TC, two-pass retest, buildId gate)
  5. **Close**: tracker close/return (`jira_close_issue.py` / `jira_return_in_progress.py`, or `github_close_issue.py` / `github_return_to_dev.py`) on every terminal ticket
  6. **Evidence**: E2E recording (`record_and_attach.sh`) + screenshot for filed bugs, unless exempt
  7. **New tests**: persist/extend the regression TC (`ticket_tc.sh`) and, for every confirmed defect, a regression test referencing its bug id
  8. **Drain the backlog** (see below) — before the gate, not after
  9. `factory_tick_gate.sh` — must print `GATE OPEN`
  10. `tick_end` + `run.md` update
  **Forbidden, always:** status-only summaries, "no follow-ups needed", "nothing to do" without running `qa_scope.sh`, or deferring any part of the above to the next wake. The user-facing reply is a **brief result after full execution**, never a substitute for it.
- **Drain the backlog — never stop at one ticket or one scope pass.** A tick is not bounded to "one ticket" or "one scan": after resolving every ticket from a scope scan, **re-run `qa_scope.sh <slug> --log --shell` again** — before `factory_tick_gate.sh`, not after. If the fresh scan returns more (or different) tickets — including new `impl-qa`/`impl-dev` To Do items freed up by work just completed — **keep going, ticket by ticket, in the same session**, then re-scan again. Only stop draining when a scan genuinely returns nothing actionable (count=0, or every remaining item is a legitimate dev-owned `SKIP_DEV`); then log `backlog_drained` and run the gate. Do not artificially cap work at one ticket per tick and defer the rest to the next timer wake. **Gate enforced:** this requirement is checked against *every* ticket resolved anywhere in the tick (union of keys across every scope_check), not just whatever the final scan's keys happen to be — so it still applies after a correct drain makes resolved tickets drop out of the latest scan.
- **Teams tick notify (optional):** `qa_scope.sh --log` (Jira path) posts a Teams Adaptive Card (scope + next wake) when `QA_FACTORY_TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL` is set — use the same Power Automate URL as Hephaestus for the same channel. Unset = quiet. Real delivery failures print `QA_TICK_NOTIFY_FAILED`.
- **Scope scan — all tickets per tick, repeated until drained:** query the tracker for every in-scope Validate/Testing (or equivalent) ticket and run full machine DoD on **each** before ending the tick; never tunnel on one ticket while others remain in scope; re-scan after resolving to catch newly-appeared work (skill `qa-loop`).
  - **Same-tick completion:** autotake / feature retest with `retest_attempted=true` ⇒ **Done** or **FAIL** / **RETURN_DEV** same session. **`impl-qa` full charters → marathon mode** (work until Done; no `tick_end`/re-arm; dev scope frozen).
  - **DoD gate before tick_end:** `./scripts/factory_tick_gate.sh <slug>` must exit 0. **Marathon** (when `marathon_start` logged this tick): rejects `tick_end` until `impl-qa` → **Done**; dev tickets frozen until then. Without `marathon_start`, slice-mode **`QA_CONTINUE`** may open the gate. Rejects **`SKIP_DEV` on `impl-qa`**, **`QA_CONTINUE` during marathon**, and **`SKIP_DEV` on Validate/Testing** (skill `qa-loop`, `factory/schema.md`).
  - **Auto-accept (Validate/Testing → Done)** ONLY when the machine DoD is met: (1) retest two-pass PASS against the canonical source; (2) **STG buildId gate** — `scripts/stg_buildid.sh <slug> <handoff-sha>` returns **MATCH** or **MATCH_AHEAD** (live STG equals handoff, or is ahead on the same branch and includes the handoff commit via git ancestry; skip only for projects with no STG configured); (3) mandatory E2E recording attached (pure-CI/pipeline tickets exempt); (4) verdict is not `needs-human`; (5) **skill `qa-verdict-review`** — write `verdict-review-<KEY>.md`, pass `check_verdict_review.sh`, ledger `verdict_review=pass` **before** `jira_close_issue.py` / `github_close_issue.py` (those scripts exit 4 without it; FAIL/RETURN same rule). **MISMATCH** / **MISMATCH_BEHIND** ⇒ do NOT Done; comment expected-vs-actual buildId. 
  - **Auto-file CONFIRMED bugs** unattended (evidence + `confirmed-defect` verdict), deduped first; NEVER auto-file `works-as-specified`/`cannot-reproduce`/`needs-human`. Every filed bug MUST include labels **`confirmed-defect`** and **`impl-dev`** (dev factory pickup) — `create_bug_issue.py` → `create_jira_issue.py` (Jira) or `github_create_issue.py` (GitHub Issues) adds `impl-dev` automatically when `confirmed-defect` is present; use `--no-impl-dev` only for rare exceptions. On **github_issues** projects, product defects are **separate issues** (not only `QA RETURN` on the feature ticket).
  - **Retest FAIL handoff (mandatory):** before any scope retest, run `scripts/openspec_read.sh` and validate PF/TC against OpenSpec WHEN/THEN. On **FAIL** or **RETURN_DEV**, fill `templates/retest-fail-dev-handoff.md` and post via `jira_return_in_progress.py --handoff-file` (Jira) or `github_return_to_dev.py` with `--dev-ticket` (GitHub). **Filed bugs require screenshot + recording on the tracker bug key** (`bug_recording_attached=true`, `bug_screenshot_attached=true` in `dod_check`). Gate requires `openspec_read=true`, `openspec_req` or `openspec_scenario`, and `dev_handoff=<path>`.
  - **`needs-human`**: ambiguous requirement, policy uncertainty, or destructive/irreversible action → do NOT auto-close/auto-act; leave the ticket and surface it to the user.
- Never commit secrets — they live in gitignored `projects/<slug>/.secrets/`.
- Report is not "done" until full acceptance coverage exists — smoke passing ≠ accepted.

Procedural how-to lives in skills: `qa-runs`, `qa-phases`, `qa-loop`, `qa-openspec`, `qa-server`, `qa-jira`
(under `qa-agent/.cursor/skills/`). The portable spine is `qa-agent/AGENTS.md`.

After changing any engine script, rule, skill, or template, run `bash tests/run_tests.sh`
(offline self-tests) and keep it green before relying on the change. Before opening a PR,
run `bash scripts/pre_merge_check.sh` (skill `qa-code-review`). If Code Review fails,
follow `.cursor/rules/cr-autofix.mdc` and run `bash scripts/cr_autofix.sh` until the gate opens.
